    "score_when_query_uses_pct20_encoding_two_locations": 92.2,
    "why_92_2_vs_88_2": "SQLI-006 has Severity.CRITICAL (weight 90.0) and confidence 0.98, giving a single-match base score of 90.0 * 0.98 = 88.2. In RealMultiRoundWAFEvaluator (fix-001), urllib.parse.urlencode encodes spaces as '+' ('category_id=105+OR+17-7%3D10'): InputNormalizer uses urllib.parse.unquote (keeping '+' in location_key='raw_query'), while urllib.parse.parse_qs decodes '+' to spaces on location_key='category_id', so SQLI-006 matches ONCE (score = 88.2). When spaces are percent-encoded as '%20' ('category_id=105%20OR%2017-7%3D10', as in fix-002's standalone probe), unquote decodes '%20' on location_key='raw_query' AND parse_qs decodes location_key='category_id'; gateway/app/security/engine.py:49-87 deduplicates by (rule_id, location, location_key), recording 2 distinct location matches ('raw_query' and 'category_id') and adding RuleScorer's +4.0 multi_match_bonus (scoring.py:36-37): 88.2 + 4.0 = 92.2.",
    "distinct_location_matches_on_pct20": [
